ame>[4].fLength</Name><Value>3.96</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[4].fStartValue</Name><Value>8000</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[4].fEndValue</Name><Value>11960</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5].nTrackNumber</Name><Value>5</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5].fXPosition</Name><Value>15.4</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5].fLength</Name><Value>4</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5].fStartValue</Name><Value>1267000</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5].fEndValue</Name><Value>1271000</Value></SubItem></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>1920</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fRatio</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>1984</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fLastPosition</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Extrapolation variables ]]></Comment><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>2048</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fVelocity</Name><Type>LREAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><BitOffs>2112</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFirstCycle</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>2176</BitOffs><Default><Bool>true</Bool></Default></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>ST_Track_Segment</Name><BitSize>160</BitSize><SubItem><Name>iID</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ track number]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rStart</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ local start of barcode]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rEnd</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ local end of barcode]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rAbsoluteStart</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ x_position]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rAbsoluteEnd</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ x_position + length]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_EHC_Converter</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
    ============================================================================
    FB_EHC_Converter
    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Converts a *relative* barcode/tape reading into an *absolute* track position,
    using a table of track segments. This is a clean, self-contained rewrite of
    the original EHW converter (EHWConverter + EHWFindPosition + EHWCheckRange +
    EHWCalculatePosition + EHWCheckValid). The LOGIC is intentionally identical to
    the original; only the structure, typing and documentation have been cleaned
    up. No sensor / transport / process-image code lives here on purpose.

    CORE IDEA (unchanged from the original):
      The tape repeats per segment, so a raw reading is only meaningful *within*
      a segment. The converter therefore works in two modes:

        1. ACQUISITION  (no valid previous segment, or after a reset)
           Linear-scan the whole table to find the segment whose local span
           contains the reading. This is the "cold start" / re-find.

        2. TRACKING     (we already know roughly where we are)
           Only look at the current segment and its nearer neighbour. If neither
           contains the reading, dead-reckon forward using the velocity input.
           This is cheap and robust against momentary bad reads.

      A separate, stricter band check (CheckValid) reports whether the current
      reading sits comfortably inside the segment (not near a seam), independent
      of whether a position could be produced.

    SEGMENT DIRECTION (unchanged from the original):
      A segment may count *up* (rStart < rEnd) or *down* (rStart > rEnd) along the
      tape. All band / position math handles both directions.

    CONVENTIONS / ASSUMPTIONS:
      - Track IDs are 1..C_SEGMENT_COUNT and EQUAL the array index. The original
        code indexed the array by track id, so we keep that 1:1 mapping. iID is
        kept in the struct for readability but the index is authoritative.
      - iTrackId = -1 means "no segment found / not localised".
      - The velocity dead-reckon term reproduces the original exactly
        (rAbsolute + rVelocity / 1000.0 per call). See note at that line — it is a
        per-call increment, not a per-second one; kept as-is to preserve behaviour.

    USAGE:
      fbEhc(rBarcode := <reading>, rVelocity := <vel>, bReset := <reset>);
      // fbEhc.rAbsolutePos, fbEhc.iTrackId, fbEhc.bValid, fbEhc.bExtrapolating
    ============================================================================
]]></Comment><BitSize>4992</BitSize><SubItem><Name>rBarcode</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Current RELATIVE reading from the tape [tape units]]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rVelocity</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Current velocity, used only for dead-reckoning fallback]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bReset</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Rising/level reset: forces a fresh ACQUISITION next scan]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rAbsolutePos</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Calculated ABSOLUTE position along the track, or -1.0 if not found]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>iTrackId</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Current segment id (= array index), or -1 if not localised]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bValid</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE if the reading sits safely inside the segment (strict band)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>208</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bAcquiring</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE while in ACQUISITION (full-scan) mode]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>216</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bExtrapolating</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE when position was dead-reckoned from velocity (no in-range segment)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>224</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>C_SEGMENT_COUNT</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Number of track segments in the table below]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>240</BitOffs><Default><Value>28</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>C_RANGE_GUARD</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Guard band for ACQUISITION/TRACKING in-range test (original: 0.05)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>256</BitOffs><Default><Value>0.05</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>C_VALID_GUARD</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Guard band for the stricter validity test       (original: 0.2)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>288</BitOffs><Default><Value>0.2</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>C_FAR</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ "Effectively infinite" distance used to veto a clamped neighbour]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>320</BitOffs><Default><Value>5000</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>C_NONE</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Sentinel: no segment]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>352</BitOffs><Default><Value>-1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>aTracks</Name><Type>ST_Track_Segment</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>28</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ --- Track table -------------------------------------------------------
       Real survey values, taken from GVL_PROP_BARCODE_EHW.TrackSegmentsRaw1.
       Mapping ST_Track_Segment_Raw -> ST_Track_Segment:
         iID            := iTrackNumber           (1..N, == array index)
         rStart         := rStartValue            (local barcode span start)
         rEnd           := rEndValue              (local barcode span end)
         rAbsoluteStart := iXPosition             (absolute span start [m])
         rAbsoluteEnd   := iXPosition + iLength   (absolute span end   [m])
       Each segment has a DISTINCT barcode range (what the matching relies on).
       Small physical gaps exist between some segments (e.g. 16.2 -> 16.4);
       the converter dead-reckons across them.                              ]]></Comment><BitSize>4480</BitSize><BitOffs>384</BitOffs><Default><SubItem><Name>[1].iID</Name><Value>1</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[1].rStart</Name><Value>640</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[1].rEnd</Name><Value>644</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[1].rAbsoluteStart</Name><Value>0</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[1].rAbsoluteEnd</Name><Value>4</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[2].iID</Name><Value>2</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[2].rStart</Name><Value>628</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[2].rEnd</Name><Value>632</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[2].rAbsoluteStart</Name><Value>4</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[2].rAbsoluteEnd</Name><Value>8</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[3].iID</Name><Value>3</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[3].rStart</Name><Value>636</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[3].rEnd</Name><Value>640</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[3].rAbsoluteStart</Name><Value>8</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[3].rAbsoluteEnd</Name><Value>12</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[4].iID</Name><Value>4</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[4].rStart</Name><Value>304.6</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[4].rEnd</Name><Value>308.8</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[4].rAbsoluteStart</Name><Value>12</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[4].rAbsoluteEnd</Name><Value>16.2</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5].iID</Name><Value>5</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5].rStart</Name><Value>212.2</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5].rEnd</Name><Value>216.4</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5].rAbsoluteStart</Name><Value>16.4</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5].rAbsoluteEnd</Name><Value>20.6</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[6].iID</Name><Value>6</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[6].rStart</Name><Value>660</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[6].rEnd</Name><Value>664</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[6].rAbsoluteStart</Name><Value>20.6</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[6].rAbsoluteEnd</Name><Value>24.6</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name