ame><Value>26</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[26].rStart</Name><Value>548</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[26].rEnd</Name><Value>552</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[26].rAbsoluteStart</Name><Value>101.2</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[26].rAbsoluteEnd</Name><Value>105.2</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[27].iID</Name><Value>27</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[27].rStart</Name><Value>876</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[27].rEnd</Name><Value>880</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[27].rAbsoluteStart</Name><Value>105.2</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[27].rAbsoluteEnd</Name><Value>109.2</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[28].iID</Name><Value>28</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[28].rStart</Name><Value>287.8</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[28].rEnd</Name><Value>292</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[28].rAbsoluteStart</Name><Value>109.2</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[28].rAbsoluteEnd</Name><Value>113.4</Value></SubItem></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>iTrackIdPrev</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ -1 forces ACQUISITION on the first scan]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>4864</BitOffs><Default><Value>-1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rAbsolutePrev</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Last absolute position (seed for tracking / dead-reckoning)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>4896</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>iFound</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Scratch: index returned by Acquire()]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>4928</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>InBand</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
    Is the reading inside this segment's local span, minus a guard band?
    Handles both segment directions (up: rStart<rEnd, down: rStart>rEnd).
    Unifies the original EHWCheckRange (guard 0.05) and EHWCheckValid (guard 0.2),
    which were identical apart from the guard value.
]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>rReading</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ current relative reading]]></Comment><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ts</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ segment to test against]]></Comment><Type>ST_Track_Segment</Type><BitSize>160</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>rGuard</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ guard band to keep away from the seams]]></Comment><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>Track</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
    TRACKING step: refine id + absolute position when we already have a fix.
    Mirrors EHWFindPosition:
      - Consider the previous and next segments (clamped at the table ends).
      - Pick the neighbour ("other") that is nearer to our current absolute pos.
      - If the reading falls in that neighbour -> hand over to it.
      - Else if it still falls in the current segment -> stay, recompute.
      - Else -> dead-reckon forward from velocity (sets bExtrapolating).
    iId and rAbsolute are updated in place.
]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>rReading</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>rVelocity</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>iId</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ current segment id (= index); refined in place]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">INT</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>rAbsolute</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ current absolute position; refined in place]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">REAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Local><Name>iPrev</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>iNext</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>iOther</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>rDistPrev</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>rDistNext</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>CalcPosition</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
    Map a local reading to an absolute track position within a segment.
    Mirrors EHWCalculatePosition, handling both segment directions.
]]></Comment><ReturnType>REAL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>32</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>rReading</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ts</Name><Type>ST_Track_Segment</Type><BitSize>160</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>Acquire</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
    ACQUISITION scan: walk the whole table and return the index of the first
    segment whose local span contains the reading, or C_NONE (-1) if none.
    Same result as the original EHWConverter WHILE-loop, written cleanly.
]]></Comment><ReturnType>INT</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>16</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>rReading</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Local><Name>i</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local></Method><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name>FB_EHC_Converter_Test</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
    ============================================================================
    FB_EHC_Converter
    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Converts a *relative* barcode/tape reading into an *absolute* track position,
    using a table of track segments. This is a clean, self-contained rewrite of
    the original EHW converter (EHWConverter + EHWFindPosition + EHWCheckRange +
    EHWCalculatePosition + EHWCheckValid). The LOGIC is intentionally identical to
    the original; only the structure, typing and documentation have been cleaned
    up. No sensor / transport / process-image code lives here on purpose.

    CORE IDEA (unchanged from the original):
      The tape repeats per segment, so a raw reading is only meaningful *within*
      a segment. The converter therefore works in two modes:

        1. ACQUISITION  (no valid previous segment, or after a reset)
           Linear-scan the whole table to find the segment whose local span
           contains the reading. This is the "cold start" / re-find.

        2. TRACKING     (we already know roughly where we are)
           Only look at the current segment and its nearer neighbour. If neither
           contains the reading, dead-reckon forward using the velocity input.
           This is cheap and robust against momentary bad reads.

      A separate, stricter band check (CheckValid) reports whether the current
      reading sits comfortably inside the segment (not near a seam), independent
      of whether a position could be produced.

    SEGMENT DIRECTION (unchanged from the original):
      A segment may count *up* (rStart < rEnd) or *down* (rStart > rEnd) along the
      tape. All band / position math handles both directions.

    CONVENTIONS / ASSUMPTIONS:
      - Track IDs are 1..C_SEGMENT_COUNT and EQUAL the array index. The original
        code indexed the array by track id, so we keep that 1:1 mapping. iID is
        kept in the struct for readability but the index is authoritative.
      - iTrackId = -1 means "no segment found / not localised".
      - The velocity dead-reckon term reproduces the original exactly
        (rAbsolute + rVelocity / 1000.0 per call). See note at that line — it is a
        per-call increment, not a per-second one; kept as-is to preserve behaviour.

    USAGE:
      fbEhc(rBarcode := <reading>, rVelocity := <vel>, bReset := <reset>);
      // fbEhc.rAbsolutePos, fbEhc.iTrackId, fbEhc.bValid, fbEhc.bExtrapolating
    ============================================================================
]]></Comment><BitSize>1280</BitSize><SubItem><Name>rBarcode</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Current RELATIVE reading from the tape [tape units]]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rVelocity</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Current velocity, used only for dead-reckoning fallback]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bReset</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Rising/level reset: forces a fresh ACQUISITION next scan]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rAbsolutePos</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Calculated ABSOLUTE position along the track, or -1.0 if not found]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>iTrackId</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Current segment id (= array index), or -1 if not localised]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bValid</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE if the reading sits safely inside the segment (strict band)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>208</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bAcquiring</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE while in ACQUISITION (full-scan) mode]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>216</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bExtrapolating</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ TRUE when position was dead-reckoned from velocity (no in-range segment)]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>224</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>C_SEGMENT_COUNT</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Number of track segments in the table below]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>240</BitOffs><Default><Value>5</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>C_RANGE_GUARD</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Guard band for ACQUISITION/TRACKING in-range test (original: 0.05)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>256</BitOffs><Default><Value>0.05</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>C_VALID_GUARD</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Guard band for the stricter validity test       (original: 0.2)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>288</BitOffs><Default><Value>0.2</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>C_FAR</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ "Effectively infinite" distance used to veto a clamped neighbour]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>320</BitOffs><Default><Value>5000</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>C_NONE</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Sentinel: no segment]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>352</BitOffs><Default><Value>-1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>aTracks</Name><Type>ST_Track_Segment</Type><ArrayInfo><LBound>1</LBound><Elements>5</Elements></ArrayInfo><Comment><![CDATA[ --- Track table -------------------------------------------------------
       Fill in the real survey values. Each segment carries its LOCAL span on
       the tape (rStart..rEnd) and the ABSOLUTE span on the track
       (rAbsoluteStart..rAbsoluteEnd). Keep iID equal to the array index.
       Placeholder values below — replace with the real layout.            ]]></Comment><BitSize>800</BitSize><BitOffs>384</BitOffs><Default><SubItem><Name>[1].iID</Name><Value>1</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[1].rStart</Name><Value>1255160</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[1].rEnd</Name><Value>1258560</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[1].rAbsoluteStart</Name><Value>0</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[1].rAbsoluteEnd</Name><Value>3.4</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[2].iID</Name><Value>2</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[2].rStart</Name><Value>0</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[2].rEnd</Name><Value>4000</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[2].rAbsoluteStart</Name><Value>3.4</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[2].rAbsoluteEnd</Name><Value>7.4</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[3].iID</Name><Value>3</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[3].rStart</Name><Value>4000</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[3].rEnd</Name><Value>8000</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[3].rAbsoluteStart</Name><Value>7.4</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[3].rAbsoluteEnd</Name><Value>11.4</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[4].iID</Name><Value>4</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[4].rStart</Name><Value>8000</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[4].rEnd</Name><Value>11960</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[4].rAbsoluteStart</Name><Value>11.4</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[4].rAbsoluteEnd</Name><Value>15.36</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5].iID</Name><Value>5</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5].rStart</Name><Value>1267000</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5].rEnd</Name><Value>1271000</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5].rAbsoluteStart</Name><Value>15.4</Value></SubItem><SubItem><Name>[5].rAbsoluteEnd</Name><Value>19.6</Value></SubItem></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>iTrackIdPrev</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ -1 forces ACQUISITION on the first scan]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>1184</BitOffs><Default><Value>-1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>rAbsolutePrev</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Last absolute position (seed for tracking / dead-reckoning)]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>1216</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>iFound</Name><Type>INT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Scratch: index returned by Acquire()]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>1248</BitOffs></SubItem><Method><Name>InBand</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
    Is the reading inside this segment's local span, minus a guard band?
    Handles both segment directions (up: rStart<rEnd, down: rStart>rEnd).
    Unifies the original EHWCheckRange (guard 0.05) and EHWCheckValid (guard 0.2),
    which were identical apart from the guard value.
]]></Comment><ReturnType>BOOL</ReturnType><ReturnBitSize>8</ReturnBitSize><Parameter><Name>rReading</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ current relative reading]]></Comment><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>ts</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ segment to test against]]></Comment><Type>ST_Track_Segment</Type><BitSize>160</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>rGuard</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ guard band to keep away from the seams]]></Comment><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter></Method><Method><Name>Track</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
    TRACKING step: refine id + absolute position when we already have a fix.
    Mirrors EHWFindPosition:
      - Consider the previous and next segments (clamped at the table ends).
      - Pick the neighbour ("other") that is nearer to our current absolute pos.
      - If the reading falls in that neighbour -> hand over to it.
      - Else if it still falls in the current segment -> stay, recompute.
      - Else -> dead-reckon forward from velocity (sets bExtrapolating).
    iId and rAbsolute are updated in place.
]]></Comment><Parameter><Name>rReading</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>rVelocity</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Parameter><Parameter><Name>iId</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ current segment id (= index); refined in place]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">INT</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Parameter><Name>rAbsolute</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ current absolute position; refined in place]]></Comment><Type ReferenceTo="true">REAL</Type><BitSize>64</BitSize><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>InOut</Value></Property></Properties></Parameter><Local><Name>iPrev</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>iNext</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>iOther</Name><Type>INT</Type><BitSize>16</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>rDistPrev</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local><Local><Name>rDistNext</Name><Type>REAL</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize></Local></Method><Method><Name>CalcPosition</Name><Comment><![CDATA[
